{\color{blue}A separate study evaluates the corrected objective from the supplied original workbooks under a fixed chronological protocol. Model fitting uses 1 January--31 December 2019. The first quarter of 2020 is reserved as a validation period but is not used for parameter selection; April--June 2020 supplies interval calibration labels, and July--December 2020 supplies test labels. All boundaries are left-inclusive and right-exclusive at midnight. The forecast horizon is 15 minutes: each input contains the preceding 24 observations, with consecutive input-to-input and last-input-to-target intervals of exactly 15 minutes. Past input observations may cross a split boundary; fitting, calibration, and test target timestamps do not overlap.}

{\color{blue}The input schema common to all six sites comprises four wind speeds, temperature, and sine/cosine encodings of four wind directions, giving 13 features per time step and 312 flattened inputs. Times written as 24:00 are normalized to the next day; all rows sharing an ambiguous duplicate timestamp are removed before chronological sorting. Missing codes ($-99$), nonfinite values, all-zero meteorological records, negative wind speeds, and directions outside $[0,360]$ are treated as missing covariates. Targets with missing power, hub wind, or temperature and windows with non-15-minute gaps are excluded by fixed rules. Other power values, including negative or above-capacity observations, are retained. Missing input values are replaced by lag-specific fitting means; an entirely missing coordinate uses zero. Feature standardization and capacity-normalized label standardization use only the observations actually fitted in that branch, excluding unused target labels in scarcity experiments. No future-value filling, clipping, or error-based exclusions are applied. The original files are preserved, although their upstream measurement and processing history is not fully documented.}

{\color{blue}Domain thresholds use valid meteorological observations from 2019 only. Farm~6 thresholds are 15.43\,m/s for wind and 10.24/31.36\,$^\circ$C for temperature; its training set contains 32,832 source and 2,076 target windows. Table~\ref{tab:chronological_counts} reports all six sites. Test membership is determined retrospectively from observed target-time weather; this protocol does not forecast event onset. The time split, missing-value rules, model settings, and comparison grids were fixed before any fit in this study. Earlier use of this public dataset means that chronological separation should not be interpreted as evaluation on a previously unseen dataset.}

